.TH SYNCSPACE 1 "@RELEASE_DATE@" "SyncSpace @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
syncspace \- open the SyncSpace native local-file-transfer application
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B syncspace
.br
.B syncspace
.RI [ --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
SyncSpace opens a dedicated desktop window for sending files directly between
trusted devices on the same local network. It does not open a browser, require
an account, or upload files to a cloud relay.
.PP
The desktop process owns a private companion backend for discovery, pairing,
encrypted transfers, settings, and history. Launching SyncSpace again focuses
the existing window instead of starting another backend.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
Print the installed SyncSpace version without opening the window.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/SyncSpace
Default identity, trust database, settings, and transfer working data.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/SyncSpace/logs/desktop-backend.log
Desktop companion-backend log.
.TP
.I $HOME/Downloads/SyncSpace
Default received-file directory for a new profile.
